            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Taroky is a tarot game for 4 players played mainly in the Czech Republic (especially Moravia) and Slovakia. 54-card pack: 22 permanent trumps (taroky)â€”Å¡kÃ½z, XXI (mond) down to I (pagÃ¡t)â€”plus four suits of eight cards each. Twelve cards each, six in talon; play anticlockwise. Teams are one vs three or two vs two by bidding. Bidder often calls XIX for partner. Point-trick game: follow suit, trump if void; count card points in tricks. Bonuses for declared combinations and last trick with pagÃ¡t. No-bid game VarÅ¡ava: avoid winning points.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Country/Region of Origin: Europe\nTime Period: Early 1900s\nHistorical Development: The game evolved from traditional card games in the region\nCultural Significance: Popular social and family game',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Four players (or five with one sitting out per deal). Play is anticlockwise. Teams are one vs three or two vs two, determined by bidding; in two vs two the bidder calls a tarok (usually XIX) and its holder becomes the declarer's partner.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '54-card tarok pack (22 trumps + 8 per suit)',
